    "prompt": "Create a five-panel cinematic storyboard grid for a dog food commercial, arranged in two rows: three panels on top and two wider panels below. Each panel is labeled with a white number in the upper-left corner (01 through 05). The overall look is photorealistic, warm-toned, shallow depth of field, like a high-end TV spot.\n\nPanel 01: A Shiba Inu with reddish-tan fur lies flat on its belly on a wooden floor at the edge of a rug, chin resting down, eyes open and looking forward with a patient, slightly sad expression. Background shows a cozy living room softly out of focus: a green sofa, a side table with a lamp, a wall clock, and houseplants.\n\nPanel 02: An extreme close-up of the same Shiba Inu's head, focusing on one erect pointed ear and one dark glossy eye, with a few motion-blur lines near the ear suggesting it just perked up or twitched toward a sound. Warm bokeh light glows behind.\n\nPanel 03: A young East Asian woman with short dark bobbed hair walks along an outdoor city street at dusk, wearing a beige wool coat over a gray sweater and carrying a shoulder bag. She looks upward with a faint hopeful smile. Behind her are apartment buildings with lit windows, streetlights, blurred pedestrians, and a train-station-like canopy.\n\nPanel 04: Interior view from behind the Shiba Inu standing on the rug, tail curled up, ears alert, staring intently at the front door where a thin sliver of bright light appears beneath it, signaling someone arriving. A pair of shoes sits by the entryway; the living room furniture frames the left side.\n\nPanel 05: Close-up of a hand in a cream knit sleeve turning a key in a metal door lock cylinder, while the Shiba Inu's face peeks eagerly into frame from behind the arm, eyes fixed forward with anticipation.\n\nKeep all five panels visually consistent in lighting, color grade, and the same dog character. No text other than the numbered labels.",
