    "prompt": "Goal: Create a realistic iPhone photo library screenshot featuring a grid of cat photos.\nCanvas: Vertical mobile aspect ratio (9:16) mimicking an iOS interface.\nLayout: A standard iOS status bar at the top, a header with Japanese text, a 3x3 grid of square images in the center, and a bottom navigation bar with four icons.\nSections:\n- Top Bar: Status bar showing time '23:48', signal bars, wifi icon, and battery. Below that, a large bold title on the left reading 'ライブラリ' (Library). On the right, a blue pill-shaped button reading '選択' (Select) and a three-dot menu icon.\n- Image Grid: Nine distinct photos arranged in a 3x3 grid. All photos feature the same tabby and white cat wearing a small green collar or bib.\n  - Row 1: Close-up of face licking nose; sitting next to a food bowl; sitting by a window looking down.\n  - Row 2: Butt sticking out from behind a curtain; playing with a feather toy; lying head-down on a laptop keyboard.\n  - Row 3: Drinking water from a faucet; stretching one paw up while lying down; sleeping inside a cardboard box.\n- Bottom Bar: Four navigation icons with labels below them. Left to right: Blue 'Photos' icon labeled 'ライブラリ' (Library), grey heart icon labeled 'For You', grey stack icon labeled 'アルバム' (Albums), grey magnifying glass labeled '検索' (Search).\nVisual style: Photorealistic UI mockup. The photos within the grid should look like high-quality amateur pet photography—natural lighting, slightly candid angles, warm tones.\nText content: Preserve all Japanese text exactly as described in the layout sections.",
